(5287440, 767713, 46168, '<td valign="top">I''m so happy!!  Thanks everyone who voted this up.  This is my playful little sheltie-poo, Dougie, and the shepherd is Elsa.   We have tons of snow, so great photo ops to isolate subjects against the snowbanks.  This was basically basic editing!  Thanks, Lynne, for your valuable input, as always!</td>', 'I''m so happy!!  Thanks everyone who voted this up.  This is my playful little sheltie-poo, Dougie, and the shepherd is Elsa.   We have tons of snow, so great photo ops to isolate subjects against the snowbanks.  This was basically basic editing!  Thanks, Lynne, for your valuable input, as always!', '2009-03-04 07:44:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(5287442, 768104, 103601, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by patentmike:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice idea, but without the title, I couldn''t be sure it was an ax. Why is the grass the only ting in focus? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>i think because the whole stump was shaking from the ax striking the log. in hind site, i should have composed the shot a lot differently, but i didn''t really want to get myself in frame.<br/> <br/>thanks for the comments everyone :)</td>', 'Originally posted by patentmike: Nice idea, but without the title, I couldn''t be sure it was an ax. Why is the grass the only ting in focus?   i think because the whole stump was shaking from the ax striking the log. in hind site, i should have composed the shot a lot differently, but i didn''t really want to get myself in frame. thanks for the comments everyone :)', '2009-03-04 07:46:41.000000', NULL, 0),
