(5294881, 766492, 74559, '<td valign="top">Well I''ll tell you what, you ought to join in the side challenge going on right now <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=877290" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here</a>; folks there are a bit more appreciative of blur than in voted challenges :-) Actually I think this is pretty cool; I really love the tree blur, and that little tiny house in all that darkness. I like the street blur too, it''s hard to see but there. An interesting way to brighten up the shadows a bit would be to add a light colored scratchy texture as a layer then set to overlay mode (in photoshop). Anyway, I like it!</td>', 'Well I''ll tell you what, you ought to join in the side challenge going on right now here; folks there are a bit more appreciative of blur than in voted challenges :-) Actually I think this is pretty cool; I really love the tree blur, and that little tiny house in all that darkness. I like the street blur too, it''s hard to see but there. An interesting way to brighten up the shadows a bit would be to add a light colored scratchy texture as a layer then set to overlay mode (in photoshop). Anyway, I like it!', '2009-03-07 22:04:13.000000', NULL, 0),
